<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03LV">Corollary <span data-tag="03LV">7.4.2.15</span>.</a> Let $\kappa $ be an uncountable cardinal and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a left fibration of $\infty $-categories which is essentially $\kappa $-small. Then a functor $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ is a covariant transport representation for $U$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="028V" href="/tag/028V">5.6.5.1</a>) if and only if it is a left Kan extension of the constant functor $\underline{ \Delta ^0 }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}$ along $U$. </p>
</article>
